revise(10,[('Convert H×W×C to C×H×W, then add a leading batch axis to obtain N×C×H×W.','The supplied array layout and the documented batched Conv2d argument order require moving the channel axis before height/width.'),('Add a leading batch axis only, leaving the tensor as N×H×W×C.','That retains channels last as the logical axis order, unlike the specified Conv2d input convention.'),('Swap height and width, then add a batch axis to obtain N×W×H×C.','This swaps spatial dimensions while still leaving the channel axis in the wrong position.'),('Move channels first and append the batch axis, obtaining C×H×W×N.','The documented batched convention puts the batch axis first, not last.')],stem='An image array is explicitly supplied as H×W×C. To feed the standard batched PyTorch Conv2d input convention, which axis arrangement is needed?')
